{"availability":"available","full":"rishabh3354/JPG2PDF","name":"JPG2PDF","description":"Open-source image to PDF converter for Linux. Batch convert JPG, PNG, BMP, TIFF, SVG & WebP into PDF with custom page size, DPI and AES-256 encryption. Python/PyQt5, MIT.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":3,"forks":1,"created":"2021-05-24T16:54:00Z","updated":"2026-08-17T08:45:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rishabh3354.github.io/JPG2PDF/","topics":["aes-256","batch-conversion","desktop-app","flatpak","gui","image-converter","image-to-pdf","jpg-to-pdf","linux-app","open-source","pdf","pdf-converter","pdf-generator","pikepdf","pillow","png-to-pdf","pyqt5","python","qt5","snap"],"demo":"https://rishabh3354.github.io/JPG2PDF/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:01:20.004Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T11:01:20.004Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T11:01:20.004Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:01:20.004Z","stars":3,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["JPEG2PDF is a fast, offline image-to-PDF converter for Linux. Batch convert JPG, PNG, BMP, GIF, TIFF, SVG and WebP images into high-quality PDF documents — with page size and margin control, custom DPI, page numbering, rotation, grayscale output and AES-256 password protection. Everything runs locally; your images never leave your computer."],"features":["Batch convert — turn a whole folder of images into PDFs in one click.","One PDF or many — merge every image into a single document, or export one PDF per image.","Reorder before export — move images up and down, duplicate, or sort the queue.","Page sizes — A4, A3, A5, Letter, Legal and more, with automatic orientation.","Margins and positioning — set page margins and image placement in mm, cm, pt or inches."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rishabh3354/JPG2PDF/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3f8aa245c8b313a5320f2fa8996db6837bc7a2106e236498478a4764ccb